  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kvitlech. Logic: Banking game to 21. Key: 12 can be 12/9, Ace=1, framed 2+11=auto 21. Banker plays last.',
    Player: 'Kvitlech is a Jewish Hanukkah banking game similar to 21. 24-card deck (two sets 1-12, no suits). Get closest to 21 without busting. 12 can be 12 or 9. Ace always = 1. Banker plays last and must beat all hands.',
    objective: 'Get a card total of exactly 21, or as close as possible without exceeding it (busting).',
    gameplay: "1. Players bet against the house.\n2. Players can 'Hit' (draw more cards) one by one.\n3. If a player reaches 21, they win immediately.\n4. If they exceed 21, they are out.\n5. The Banker draws last and must beat all 'Open' hands to win their bets.",
    keyRules: [
      '24-card deck: two sets of numbers 1-12',
      'No standard suits or court cards',
      "12 can count as 12 or 9 (player's choice)",
      '1 (Ace) always counts as 1 (never 11)',
      'Framed 2s and 11s together count as automatic 21',
      'Banker plays last and must beat all remaining hands',
    ],
